# rule.require.orchestrators-as-narrative

an orchestrator reads as narrative: each line tells what happens, never how
```ts
const emails = getAllActiveUserEmails({ users: input.users });
const canAccess = isEligibleForPremiumFeatures({ user: input.user });
if (canAccess) await context.sdkEmail.sendBulk({ to: emails, subject: 'Update' });
```
never machine code: no inline `.filter(…).sort(…)` pipelines or compound booleans in the orchestrator body
enforcement: orchestrator with decode-friction = blocker
